*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* IR2110 - High and low side driver (also covers the IR2113)
* Behavioral ("functional") macromodel for LTspice.
*
* Based on:
*   International Rectifier (Infineon), "IR2110(S)PbF/IR2113(S)PbF High and
*   low side driver", Data Sheet No. PD60147 rev.V (6/3/2019)
*
* This is NOT a transistor-level model.  Every block of the Functional Block
* Diagram is reproduced by its terminal behaviour, with the numbers taken from
* the Static and Dynamic Electrical Characteristics tables (TYPICAL column)
* and from the typical curves (Figures 7..27).  The point is to simulate the
* gate drive of a half-bridge - bootstrap, dead time, UVLO, shutdown - inside
* a closed-loop converter: fast, convergent, and independent of the time step.
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* PIN ORDER  (14-lead PDIP pin order; the NC pins 4, 8 and 14 are left out)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*   1  LO    low-side gate drive output        9  VDD   logic supply
*   2  COM   low-side return                  10  HIN   high-side logic input
*   3  VCC   low-side supply                  11  SD    shutdown input
*   5  VS    high-side floating return        12  LIN   low-side logic input
*   6  VB    high-side floating supply        13  VSS   logic ground
*   7  HO    high-side gate drive output
*
*   X1 LO COM VCC VS VB HO VDD HIN SD LIN VSS IR2110
*
*   (16-lead SOIC IR2110S: same signals, different pin numbers - use the
*    same subcircuit, the port ORDER above is what matters.)
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* WHAT IS MODELLED
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  * Logic inputs HIN, LIN, SD: CMOS Schmitt triggers referred to VSS, with
*    thresholds proportional to VDD at the guaranteed limits of Figures 12B
*    and 13B: rising threshold VIH = 0.633*VDD (9.5 V at VDD = 15 V, 3.2 V at
*    5 V), falling threshold VIL = 0.40*VDD (6.0 V at 15 V, 2.0 V at 5 V).
*    750 k pull-down to VSS (IIN+ = 20 uA at 15 V), clamp diodes to VDD/VSS.
*  * Cycle-by-cycle edge-triggered shutdown: each channel has the RS latch of
*    the block diagram.  SD high turns both outputs off; when SD returns low
*    an output stays off until its input goes low and high again (Figure 1).
*  * UVLO on VCC (8.5 V / 8.2 V typ) and on VBS (8.6 V / 8.2 V typ), with
*    hysteresis.  VCC under-voltage holds LO low (level) and HO low; VBS
*    under-voltage holds HO low.  HO only comes back on the NEXT rising edge
*    of HIN after the fault clears (the high side is set by edge pulses
*    through the level shifter, so a fault resets its latch).
*  * Propagation delays (Figures 7B/7C, 8B/8C, 9B/9C, typical): ton 120 ns,
*    toff 94 ns, tsd 110 ns at VCC = VBS = VDD = 15 V, CL = 1 nF; they grow
*    at low VDD (ton/toff ~ 140/150 ns at VDD = 5 V) and shrink with VBIAS.
*    HO and LO use the same delay chain, so they are matched (MT ~ 0).
*    The delays are linear ramps - an input pulse shorter than ~ton is
*    swallowed, as in the real part.
*  * Output stages: pull-up and pull-down, I = Isat*tanh(V/V0)/tanh(2), with
*    Isat = IO+ / IO- = 2.5 A typ at 15 V, scaled with VBIAS as Figures
*    26B/27B (1.45 A at 10 V, 3.55 A at 20 V); knee V0 = VBIAS/2.  The gate
*    of each output device is ramped (pre-driver), which is what sets the
*    rise / fall time: tr 25 ns, tf 17 ns at 15 V into 1 nF (Figures 10B,
*    11B: tr falls and tf grows with VBIAS).  No cross-conduction between
*    the two output devices.  Body diodes HO-VB, VS-HO, LO-VCC, COM-LO.
*  * Quiescent currents: IQCC 180 uA, IQBS 125 uA, IQDD 15 uA typ at 15 V,
*    following the shape of Figures 17B, 18B, 19B.  Gate charge is drawn from
*    VCC (LO) and from VB (HO) - the bootstrap capacitor sees it.
*  * The logic ground VSS may sit +-5 V away from COM; everything on the logic
*    side is referred to VSS, LO to COM and HO to VS.
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* WHAT IS NOT MODELLED  (behavioural model - know the limits)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  * No temperature model (KD / KE scale the delays and edges; KD = 1.3 and
*    KE = 1.8 land within 7 % of the MAX column at 25 C).
*  * No bootstrap diode inside (the IR2110 has none - put your own).
*  * Offset supply leakage (ILK <= 50 uA at 500 V), dVs/dt immunity,
*    negative VS transients and latch-up, level-shifter dV/dt false
*    triggering: not modelled.  The 500 V / 600 V ratings are not policed.
*  * The input thresholds sit at the guaranteed limits (VIH max, VIL min);
*    a real part switches somewhere in between.
*  * With VDD - VSS below ~2.5 V the logic is considered dead and both
*    outputs are held low (not specified in the datasheet).
*  * With VBIAS under the UVLO the outputs are actively held low down to
*    0 V of supply (5 % of the normal sink strength) - the real part's
*    behaviour with a fully discharged supply is not specified.
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* PARAMETERS  (override per instance:  X1 ... IR2110 KD=1.3 KE=1.8)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*  KD       delay factor (1 = typical, ~1.3 = max column at 25 C)
*  KE       rise/fall-time factor (1 = typical, ~1.8 = max column)
*  VIHF     rising input threshold, fraction of VDD-VSS     (0.633)
*  VILF     falling input threshold, fraction of VDD-VSS    (0.40)
*  RIN      input pull-down                                 (750k)
*  CIN      input capacitance (not in the datasheet)        (2 pF)
*  COUT     HO / LO pin capacitance (not in the datasheet)  (10 pF)
*  UVCCP/N  VCC UVLO rising / falling threshold            (8.5 / 8.2 V)
*  UVBSP/N  VBS UVLO rising / falling threshold            (8.6 / 8.2 V)
*  TON, TOFF, TSD  ton / toff / tsd at VDD = VBIAS = 15 V, ns (120/94/110)
*  KBON     ton change per -5 V of VBIAS (Figure 7B)        (0.167)
*  KBOFF    toff change per -5 V of VBIAS (Figure 8B)       (0.183)
*  DON*, DOFF*  ton / toff factor at VDD = 3.5/5/10/20 V (Figures 7C, 8C)
*  TER*, TEF*   output gate ramp, ns, at VBIAS = 10/15/20 V (fitted to
*               Figures 10B / 11B)
*  TFAST    release time of the device that turns off, ns  (3)
*  TOON*, TOOF* time from the start of that ramp to 10 % / 90 % of the
*               output into 1 nF, ns (fitted; subtracted from ton / toff)
*  IO       output short-circuit current at VBIAS = 15 V, A  (2.5)
*  KIO      IO change per +5 V of VBIAS (Figures 26B/27B)   (0.42)
*  KV0      output knee as a fraction of VBIAS              (0.5)
*  IQCC, IQBS, IQDD   quiescent supply currents at 15 V     (180u 125u 15u)
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* LTspice .FRA / .AC / .OP
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* No time-dependent sources, no internal oscillator; every Schmitt trigger,
* UVLO and latch is an integrating set/reset cell with DC solutions 0 and 1
* only, and every delay or edge is a finite-slope ramp written so that its
* DC value is exact, with no kink where a node rests.  The operating point
* needs no search and the edge times move continuously with the input,
* whatever the time step.  See README.md for the loop-gain measurement of
* the closed-loop example.
*------------------------------------------------------------------------------

.SUBCKT IR2110 LO COM VCC VS VB HO VDD HIN SD LIN VSS
+ KD=1 KE=1 VIHF=0.633 VILF=0.40 RIN=750k CIN=2p COUT=10p
+ UVCCP=8.5 UVCCN=8.2 UVBSP=8.6 UVBSN=8.2
+ TON=120 TOFF=94 TSD=110 KBON=0.167 KBOFF=0.183
+ TOON10=13.9 TOON15=12.4 TOON20=11.0 TOOF10=5.6 TOOF15=9.2 TOOF20=12.5
+ DON35=1.58 DON5=1.20 DON10=1.035 DON20=0.966
+ DOFF35=2.14 DOFF5=1.56 DOFF10=1.17 DOFF20=0.76
+ TER10=75.5 TER15=69.2 TER20=57.1 TEF10=3.6 TEF15=32.1 TEF20=79.8 TFAST=3
+ IO=2.5 KIO=0.42 KV0=0.5
+ IQCC=180u IQBS=125u IQDD=15u

*==============================================================================
* SUPPLIES, UVLO
* Internal "digital" nodes are 0..1 V, referred to VSS.
* Every state bit (Schmitt triggers, UVLO, latches) is an INTEGRATING
* set/reset cell, the same construction as the UC3854 and L6599A models:
*
*     C dq/dt = G * ( S*(1-q) - R*q ),   G = 1 mA/V, C = 1 pF (1 ns)
*     S = set   OR ( q > 0.5 AND NOT reset )
*     R = reset OR ( q < 0.5 AND NOT set )
*
* With neither input active the cell is parked at 0 or 1, the only DC
* solutions are 0 and 1, and it holds its state whatever the step size.
* For a Schmitt trigger, S = (input above the upper threshold) and
* R = (input below the lower one), each a 10 mV-wide linear ramp.
*==============================================================================
Bvdd  n_vdd VSS V = max(0, V(VDD,VSS))
Bvcc  n_vcc VSS V = max(0, V(VCC,COM))
Bvbs  n_vbs VSS V = max(0, V(VB,VS))
* logic alive (not specified: below ~2.5 V of VDD the outputs are held low)
Bokd  n_okd VSS V = 0.5 + 0.5*tanh((V(n_vdd,VSS) - 2.5)/0.1)

* VCC UVLO (n_okc = 1: VCC good)
Bokcs n_okcs VSS V = max(0,min(1,(V(n_vcc,VSS)-{UVCCP})*100+0.5))
Bokcr n_okcr VSS V = max(0,min(1,({UVCCN}-V(n_vcc,VSS))*100+0.5))
Bokcq n_okcq VSS V = max(0,min(1,(V(n_okc,VSS)-0.5)*20))
Bokc  VSS n_okc I = 1m*(
+     max(V(n_okcs,VSS), V(n_okcq,VSS)*(1-V(n_okcr,VSS)))*(1-V(n_okc,VSS))
+   - max(V(n_okcr,VSS), (1-V(n_okcq,VSS))*(1-V(n_okcs,VSS)))*V(n_okc,VSS) )
Cokc  n_okc VSS 1p
Rokcg n_okc VSS 1G
* VBS UVLO (n_okb = 1: VBS good)
Bokbs n_okbs VSS V = max(0,min(1,(V(n_vbs,VSS)-{UVBSP})*100+0.5))
Bokbr n_okbr VSS V = max(0,min(1,({UVBSN}-V(n_vbs,VSS))*100+0.5))
Bokbq n_okbq VSS V = max(0,min(1,(V(n_okb,VSS)-0.5)*20))
Bokb  VSS n_okb I = 1m*(
+     max(V(n_okbs,VSS), V(n_okbq,VSS)*(1-V(n_okbr,VSS)))*(1-V(n_okb,VSS))
+   - max(V(n_okbr,VSS), (1-V(n_okbq,VSS))*(1-V(n_okbs,VSS)))*V(n_okb,VSS) )
Cokb  n_okb VSS 1p
Rokbg n_okb VSS 1G

* quiescent currents (Figures 17B, 18B, 19B)
Bqcc  VCC COM I = {IQCC}*pow(V(n_vcc,VSS)/15, 1.7)
Bqbs  VB  VS  I = {IQBS}*pow(V(n_vbs,VSS)/15, 1.7)
Bqdd  VDD VSS I = {IQDD}*(0.3*tanh(V(n_vdd,VSS)) + 0.7*V(n_vdd,VSS)/15)

*==============================================================================
* LOGIC INPUTS  HIN, LIN, SD  (Schmitt triggers referred to VSS)
*   rising threshold  VIHF*VDD,  falling threshold  VILF*VDD
*==============================================================================
.model DIR2110 D(IS=1e-15 RS=5 CJO=0)
Rih   HIN VSS {RIN}
Cih   HIN VSS {CIN}
Dihp  HIN VDD DIR2110
Dihn  VSS HIN DIR2110
Ril   LIN VSS {RIN}
Cil   LIN VSS {CIN}
Dilp  LIN VDD DIR2110
Diln  VSS LIN DIR2110
Ris   SD  VSS {RIN}
Cis   SD  VSS {CIN}
Disp  SD  VDD DIR2110
Disn  VSS SD  DIR2110

* HIN
Bxhs n_xhs VSS V = max(0,min(1,(V(HIN,VSS)-{VIHF}*V(n_vdd,VSS))*100+0.5))
Bxhr n_xhr VSS V = max(0,min(1,({VILF}*V(n_vdd,VSS)-V(HIN,VSS))*100+0.5))
Bxhq n_xhq VSS V = max(0,min(1,(V(n_xh,VSS)-0.5)*20))
Bxh  VSS n_xh I = 1m*(
+     max(V(n_xhs,VSS), V(n_xhq,VSS)*(1-V(n_xhr,VSS)))*(1-V(n_xh,VSS))
+   - max(V(n_xhr,VSS), (1-V(n_xhq,VSS))*(1-V(n_xhs,VSS)))*V(n_xh,VSS) )
Cxh  n_xh VSS 1p
Rxhg n_xh VSS 1G
* LIN
Bxls n_xls VSS V = max(0,min(1,(V(LIN,VSS)-{VIHF}*V(n_vdd,VSS))*100+0.5))
Bxlr n_xlr VSS V = max(0,min(1,({VILF}*V(n_vdd,VSS)-V(LIN,VSS))*100+0.5))
Bxlq n_xlq VSS V = max(0,min(1,(V(n_xl,VSS)-0.5)*20))
Bxl  VSS n_xl I = 1m*(
+     max(V(n_xls,VSS), V(n_xlq,VSS)*(1-V(n_xlr,VSS)))*(1-V(n_xl,VSS))
+   - max(V(n_xlr,VSS), (1-V(n_xlq,VSS))*(1-V(n_xls,VSS)))*V(n_xl,VSS) )
Cxl  n_xl VSS 1p
Rxlg n_xl VSS 1G
* SD
Bxss n_xss VSS V = max(0,min(1,(V(SD,VSS)-{VIHF}*V(n_vdd,VSS))*100+0.5))
Bxsr n_xsr VSS V = max(0,min(1,({VILF}*V(n_vdd,VSS)-V(SD,VSS))*100+0.5))
Bxsq n_xsq VSS V = max(0,min(1,(V(n_xs,VSS)-0.5)*20))
Bxs  VSS n_xs I = 1m*(
+     max(V(n_xss,VSS), V(n_xsq,VSS)*(1-V(n_xsr,VSS)))*(1-V(n_xs,VSS))
+   - max(V(n_xsr,VSS), (1-V(n_xsq,VSS))*(1-V(n_xss,VSS)))*V(n_xs,VSS) )
Cxs  n_xs VSS 1p
Rxsg n_xs VSS 1G

* SD path: extra delay tsd - toff, a lag + comparator
Bsl   VSS n_sl I = 1m*(V(n_xs,VSS) - V(n_sl,VSS))*0.693/({KD}*max(1,{TSD}-{TOFF}))
Csl   n_sl VSS 1p
Rsl   n_sl VSS 1G
Bsd   n_sd VSS V = min(1, max(0, 20*(V(n_sl,VSS) - 0.5) + 0.5))

*==============================================================================
* CYCLE-BY-CYCLE LATCHES (block diagram: one RS latch per input)
*   q = 1 blocks the channel.  Set: SD (and, for HO, a VCC or VBS fault).
*   Reset: the channel's input LOW (set wins).  So after SD (or a fault)
*   the output returns only on the next rising edge of its input.
*==============================================================================
* OR of SD and the two faults, written smooth (no kink at the rest state)
Bseth n_seth VSS V = 1 - (1-V(n_sd,VSS))*V(n_okc,VSS)*V(n_okb,VSS)
* HO latch: set by SD or a VCC / VBS fault, reset by HIN low
Bqhs n_qhs VSS V = V(n_seth,VSS)
Bqhr n_qhr VSS V = (1-V(n_xh,VSS))*(1-V(n_seth,VSS))
Bqhq n_qhq VSS V = max(0,min(1,(V(n_qh,VSS)-0.5)*20))
Bqh  VSS n_qh I = 1m*(
+     max(V(n_qhs,VSS), V(n_qhq,VSS)*(1-V(n_qhr,VSS)))*(1-V(n_qh,VSS))
+   - max(V(n_qhr,VSS), (1-V(n_qhq,VSS))*(1-V(n_qhs,VSS)))*V(n_qh,VSS) )
Cqh  n_qh VSS 1p
Rqhg n_qh VSS 1G
* LO latch: set by SD, reset by LIN low
Bqls n_qls VSS V = V(n_sd,VSS)
Bqlr n_qlr VSS V = (1-V(n_xl,VSS))*(1-V(n_sd,VSS))
Bqlq n_qlq VSS V = max(0,min(1,(V(n_ql,VSS)-0.5)*20))
Bql  VSS n_ql I = 1m*(
+     max(V(n_qls,VSS), V(n_qlq,VSS)*(1-V(n_qlr,VSS)))*(1-V(n_ql,VSS))
+   - max(V(n_qlr,VSS), (1-V(n_qlq,VSS))*(1-V(n_qls,VSS)))*V(n_ql,VSS) )
Cql  n_ql VSS 1p
Rqlg n_ql VSS 1G

* channel commands (0..1)
Bch   n_ch VSS V = V(n_xh,VSS)*(1-V(n_qh,VSS))*(1-V(n_seth,VSS))*V(n_okd,VSS)
Bcl   n_cl VSS V = V(n_xl,VSS)*(1-V(n_ql,VSS))*(1-V(n_sd,VSS))*V(n_okc,VSS)*V(n_okd,VSS)

*==============================================================================
* PROPAGATION DELAY
*   The datasheet delays (input 50 % -> output 10 % / 90 %, CL = 1 nF) are
*     ton  = TON  * KD * DON(VDD)  * (1 + KBON *(15-VBIAS)/5)
*     toff = TOFF * KD * DOFF(VDD) * (1 + KBOFF*(15-VBIAS)/5)
*   with DON/DOFF interpolated over VDD = 3.5 / 5 / 10 / 15 / 20 V (factor 1
*   at 15 V) and VBIAS clamped to 10..20 V (Figures 7B/C, 8B/C).  The part
*   of it spent in the output stage - from the start of the pre-driver ramp
*   to 10 % / 90 % of the output into 1 nF, TOON / TOOF (fitted, interpolated
*   over VBIAS) - is subtracted; the rest is the internal delay td.
*   A ramp node s follows the command at a finite slope, up at 0.5/td_on and
*   down at 0.5/td_off [1/ns], so it crosses 0.5 exactly td after the input.
*   With a heavier load than 1 nF the output part, and so ton/toff, grow.
*==============================================================================
Bdon  n_don VSS V = {DON35} + ({DON5}-({DON35}))*min(max(V(n_vdd,VSS)-3.5,0),1.5)/1.5
+   + ({DON10}-({DON5}))*min(max(V(n_vdd,VSS)-5,0),5)/5 + (1-({DON10}))*min(max(V(n_vdd,VSS)-10,0),5)/5
+   + ({DON20}-1)*min(max(V(n_vdd,VSS)-15,0),5)/5
Bdof  n_dof VSS V = {DOFF35} + ({DOFF5}-({DOFF35}))*min(max(V(n_vdd,VSS)-3.5,0),1.5)/1.5
+   + ({DOFF10}-({DOFF5}))*min(max(V(n_vdd,VSS)-5,0),5)/5 + (1-({DOFF10}))*min(max(V(n_vdd,VSS)-10,0),5)/5
+   + ({DOFF20}-1)*min(max(V(n_vdd,VSS)-15,0),5)/5
* VBIAS of each channel clamped to 10..20 V, and its output-stage share
Bkh   n_kh VSS V = min(max(V(n_vbs,VSS),10),20)
Bkl   n_kl VSS V = min(max(V(n_vcc,VSS),10),20)
Btoh  n_toh VSS V = {TOON10} + ({TOON15}-({TOON10}))*min(V(n_kh,VSS)-10,5)/5 + ({TOON20}-({TOON15}))*max(V(n_kh,VSS)-15,0)/5
Btfh  n_tfh VSS V = {TOOF10} + ({TOOF15}-({TOOF10}))*min(V(n_kh,VSS)-10,5)/5 + ({TOOF20}-({TOOF15}))*max(V(n_kh,VSS)-15,0)/5
Btol  n_tol VSS V = {TOON10} + ({TOON15}-({TOON10}))*min(V(n_kl,VSS)-10,5)/5 + ({TOON20}-({TOON15}))*max(V(n_kl,VSS)-15,0)/5
Btfl  n_tfl VSS V = {TOOF10} + ({TOOF15}-({TOOF10}))*min(V(n_kl,VSS)-10,5)/5 + ({TOOF20}-({TOOF15}))*max(V(n_kl,VSS)-15,0)/5
* slopes [1/ns] of each channel's delay ramp
Bruh  n_ruh VSS V = 0.5/max(5, {KD}*{TON}*V(n_don,VSS)*(1+{KBON}*(15-V(n_kh,VSS))/5) - {KE}*V(n_toh,VSS))
Brdh  n_rdh VSS V = 0.5/max(5, {KD}*{TOFF}*V(n_dof,VSS)*(1+{KBOFF}*(15-V(n_kh,VSS))/5) - {KE}*V(n_tfh,VSS))
Brul  n_rul VSS V = 0.5/max(5, {KD}*{TON}*V(n_don,VSS)*(1+{KBON}*(15-V(n_kl,VSS))/5) - {KE}*V(n_tol,VSS))
Brdl  n_rdl VSS V = 0.5/max(5, {KD}*{TOFF}*V(n_dof,VSS)*(1+{KBOFF}*(15-V(n_kl,VSS))/5) - {KE}*V(n_tfl,VSS))

* the ramps.  Each is a slew-limited follower written as  s = target - y:
*     C dy/dt = C d(target)/dt - G*slope(y)      (C from target to y)
* so ds/dt = slope(y): full slope beyond 0.1 of error, linear inside, the
* up and down slopes blended smoothly (tanh) through y = 0, so there is no
* kink where the node rests.  At DC y = 0 and s = target exactly - the
* operating point needs no search.
Btsh  n_tsh VSS V = V(n_ch,VSS)
Cysh  n_tsh n_ysh 1p
Bysh  n_ysh VSS I = 1m*(((V(n_ruh,VSS))+(V(n_rdh,VSS)))/2 + ((V(n_ruh,VSS))-(V(n_rdh,VSS)))/2*tanh(V(n_ysh,VSS)/0.02))*min(1,max(-1,10*V(n_ysh,VSS)))
Rysh  n_ysh VSS 1G
Bosh n_sh VSS V = V(n_tsh,VSS) - V(n_ysh,VSS)
Btsl  n_tsl VSS V = V(n_cl,VSS)
Cysl  n_tsl n_ysl 1p
Bysl  n_ysl VSS I = 1m*(((V(n_rul,VSS))+(V(n_rdl,VSS)))/2 + ((V(n_rul,VSS))-(V(n_rdl,VSS)))/2*tanh(V(n_ysl,VSS)/0.02))*min(1,max(-1,10*V(n_ysl,VSS)))
Rysl  n_ysl VSS 1G
Bosl n_slo VSS V = V(n_tsl,VSS) - V(n_ysl,VSS)

*==============================================================================
* PRE-DRIVER (gates of the two output devices)
*   d = comparator on the delay ramp.  eu drives the pull-up, ed the
*   pull-down, both 0..1.  Turning on, the pull-down is released first
*   (TFAST) and then eu ramps 0 -> 1 in TER ns; turning off, the pull-up is
*   released and ed ramps 0 -> 1 in TEF ns.  Each device only starts once
*   the other is (almost) off: no cross-conduction.  TER/TEF interpolated
*   over VBIAS = 10 / 15 / 20 V - this ramp is what sets tr and tf.
*==============================================================================
Bdh   n_dh VSS V = min(1, max(0, 50*(V(n_sh,VSS)-0.5) + 0.5))
Bdl   n_dl VSS V = min(1, max(0, 50*(V(n_slo,VSS)-0.5) + 0.5))
Bterh n_terh VSS V = {KE}*({TER10} + ({TER15}-({TER10}))*min(V(n_kh,VSS)-10,5)/5 + ({TER20}-({TER15}))*max(V(n_kh,VSS)-15,0)/5)
Btefh n_tefh VSS V = {KE}*({TEF10} + ({TEF15}-({TEF10}))*min(V(n_kh,VSS)-10,5)/5 + ({TEF20}-({TEF15}))*max(V(n_kh,VSS)-15,0)/5)
Bterl n_terl VSS V = {KE}*({TER10} + ({TER15}-({TER10}))*min(V(n_kl,VSS)-10,5)/5 + ({TER20}-({TER15}))*max(V(n_kl,VSS)-15,0)/5)
Btefl n_tefl VSS V = {KE}*({TEF10} + ({TEF15}-({TEF10}))*min(V(n_kl,VSS)-10,5)/5 + ({TEF20}-({TEF15}))*max(V(n_kl,VSS)-15,0)/5)

* pull-up only once the pull-down is off, and vice versa
Btuh  n_tuh VSS V = V(n_dh,VSS)*min(1,max(0,1.5-20*V(n_ph,VSS)))
Cyuh  n_tuh n_yuh 1p
Byuh  n_yuh VSS I = 1m*(((1/V(n_terh,VSS))+(1/{TFAST}))/2 + ((1/V(n_terh,VSS))-(1/{TFAST}))/2*tanh(V(n_yuh,VSS)/0.02))*min(1,max(-1,10*V(n_yuh,VSS)))
Ryuh  n_yuh VSS 1G
Bouh n_uh VSS V = V(n_tuh,VSS) - V(n_yuh,VSS)
Btph  n_tph VSS V = (1-V(n_dh,VSS))*min(1,max(0,1.5-20*V(n_uh,VSS)))
Cyph  n_tph n_yph 1p
Byph  n_yph VSS I = 1m*(((1/V(n_tefh,VSS))+(1/{TFAST}))/2 + ((1/V(n_tefh,VSS))-(1/{TFAST}))/2*tanh(V(n_yph,VSS)/0.02))*min(1,max(-1,10*V(n_yph,VSS)))
Ryph  n_yph VSS 1G
Boph n_ph VSS V = V(n_tph,VSS) - V(n_yph,VSS)
Btul  n_tul VSS V = V(n_dl,VSS)*min(1,max(0,1.5-20*V(n_pl,VSS)))
Cyul  n_tul n_yul 1p
Byul  n_yul VSS I = 1m*(((1/V(n_terl,VSS))+(1/{TFAST}))/2 + ((1/V(n_terl,VSS))-(1/{TFAST}))/2*tanh(V(n_yul,VSS)/0.02))*min(1,max(-1,10*V(n_yul,VSS)))
Ryul  n_yul VSS 1G
Boul n_ul VSS V = V(n_tul,VSS) - V(n_yul,VSS)
Btpl  n_tpl VSS V = (1-V(n_dl,VSS))*min(1,max(0,1.5-20*V(n_ul,VSS)))
Cypl  n_tpl n_ypl 1p
Bypl  n_ypl VSS I = 1m*(((1/V(n_tefl,VSS))+(1/{TFAST}))/2 + ((1/V(n_tefl,VSS))-(1/{TFAST}))/2*tanh(V(n_ypl,VSS)/0.02))*min(1,max(-1,10*V(n_ypl,VSS)))
Rypl  n_ypl VSS 1G
Bopl n_pl VSS V = V(n_tpl,VSS) - V(n_ypl,VSS)

*==============================================================================
* OUTPUT STAGES
*   I = s * Isat(VBIAS) * tanh(V/V0)/tanh(1/KV0),  V0 = KV0*VBIAS
*   Isat = IO*(1 + KIO*(VBIAS-15)/5), floor 5 % (keeps the output held low
*   with the supply collapsed).  VBIAS = VBS for HO, VCC for LO.
*==============================================================================
Bish  n_ish VSS V = {IO}*max(0.05, 1 + {KIO}*(V(n_vbs,VSS)-15)/5)/tanh(1/{KV0})
Bisl  n_isl VSS V = {IO}*max(0.05, 1 + {KIO}*(V(n_vcc,VSS)-15)/5)/tanh(1/{KV0})
Bv0h  n_v0h VSS V = {KV0}*max(5, V(n_vbs,VSS))
Bv0l  n_v0l VSS V = {KV0}*max(5, V(n_vcc,VSS))

Bhu   VB HO  I = V(n_uh,VSS) * V(n_ish,VSS) * tanh(V(VB,HO)/V(n_v0h,VSS))
Bhd   HO VS  I = V(n_ph,VSS) * V(n_ish,VSS) * tanh(V(HO,VS)/V(n_v0h,VSS))
Chs   HO VS  {COUT}
Dhp   HO VB  DIR2110
Dhn   VS HO  DIR2110

Blu   VCC LO I = V(n_ul,VSS) * V(n_isl,VSS) * tanh(V(VCC,LO)/V(n_v0l,VSS))
Bld   LO COM I = V(n_pl,VSS) * V(n_isl,VSS) * tanh(V(LO,COM)/V(n_v0l,VSS))
Cls   LO COM {COUT}
Dlp   LO VCC DIR2110
Dln   COM LO DIR2110

* DC paths for the floating domains (keep .op well posed with nothing
* connected; 1 Gohm is far below the 50 uA leakage spec)
Rvs   VS  VSS 1G
Rcom  COM VSS 1G
Rvb   VB  VS  100Meg
Rvc   VCC COM 100Meg

.ENDS IR2110
